{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLaplaceTransformExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLaplaceTransformExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace.exists","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L45-L62","doc":"**Existence of the categorical Laplace transform.**\n\nFor any type `A`, a `CategoricalLaplace A` term exists.  Proved below\nwith an explicit witness: the trivial transform `f ↦ (s ↦ id)`, which\npreserves the unit (`transform id s = id`) and intertwines every\n`q_conv` with composition (both sides reduce to `id`).  This\nestablishes inhabitation of the (corrected) structure; the\nmanuscript's Markov pairing against `exp_q(-s·)` is a *specific*\n`CategoricalLaplace` datum, whose construction needs the\nq-exponential grouplike + Markov-trace infrastructure not formalised\nhere.  (No `Nonempty A` is needed — the `id`-witness exists for every\n`A`, including `PEmpty`.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-laplace-exists","label":"prop:categorical-laplace-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace.monoidal_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace.monoidal_unit","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Unit preservation: `L[𝟙] = 𝟙`, where the monoidal unit of `A → A`\nunder composition is the identity `id`.  (Quantifying `one` over\n*all* functions — the previous form — together with `monoidal_mul`\nmakes the structure uninhabitable for `|A| ≥ 2`; the unit is a\nspecific object, so it is pinned to `id`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace.monoidal_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace.monoidal_mul","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Monoidal: `L[f ∗_q g] = L[f] · L[g]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace.transform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace.transform","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Pairing: `f ↦ (s ↦ ⟨exp_q(-s·), f⟩)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace","kind":"structure","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L25-L43","doc":"**Categorical Laplace transform data** (mirror of the sibling\n`def:categorical-laplace`): a monoidal functor from q-convolution\nto pointwise product, given abstractly as the Hopf pairing with the\nreal-exponential grouplike. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-laplace","label":"def:categorical-laplace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-exists.lean#L22-L23","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (mirrors the sibling definition). ","signatureChunk":0}]}